Relevant columns and their potential usage

• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."content": holds the full text of each file – this is where a JSON‑formatted file’s "require" block will be stored.  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."sample_path": lets us limit the search to filenames that are likely JSON manifest files (composer.json, package.json, etc.).  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."binary": helps exclude binary blobs (use …"binary" = FALSE).  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."size": optional guard to keep very large blobs out of ad‑hoc inspection (e.g. WHERE "size" < 50000).  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."sample_repo_name": handy for grouping or counting packages per repo.  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."sample_ref": filter by branch/tag if needed (e.g. 'refs/heads/master').  

Typical conditions you may combine  
• "sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%'                       -- PHP Composer manifests  
• "sample_path" ILIKE '%package.json%'                        -- node/npm manifests  
• "content"      ILIKE '%"require"%'                          -- quick text pre‑filter  
• "binary"       = FALSE                                      -- ignore binaries  
• "size"        < 50000                                       -- keep parsing light  

Below are 10 Snowflake SQL snippets (all with LIMIT 20) that progress from simple exploration to package extraction and frequency counting.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at some composer.json files and their raw text.
SELECT 
  "sample_repo_name",
  "sample_path",
  LEFT("content", 500) AS "preview"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%'
  AND "binary" = FALSE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Same idea for package.json (npm) manifests.
SELECT 
  "sample_repo_name",
  "sample_path",
  LEFT("content", 500) AS "preview"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%package.json%'
  AND "binary" = FALSE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Quickly verify that a "require" section exists in composer.json.
SELECT 
  "sample_repo_name",
  "sample_path"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%'
  AND "content" ILIKE '%"require"%'
  AND "binary" = FALSE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Parse composer.json and list each package under the "require" object.
SELECT 
  t."sample_repo_name",
  r.key           AS "package_name",
  r.value::STRING AS "version_constraint"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require") r
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%'
  AND t."binary" = FALSE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Count how many distinct repos use each Composer package.
SELECT 
  r.key                             AS "package_name",
  COUNT(DISTINCT t."sample_repo_name") AS "repo_count"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require") r
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%'
  AND t."binary" = FALSE
GROUP BY r.key
ORDER BY "repo_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Extract dependencies from npm package.json ("dependencies" block).
SELECT 
  t."sample_repo_name",
  d.key           AS "package_name",
  d.value::STRING AS "version_constraint"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"dependencies") d
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%package.json%'
  AND t."binary" = FALSE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Combine Composer and npm manifests, tagging the ecosystem.
SELECT 
  CASE 
    WHEN t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%' THEN 'composer'
    ELSE 'npm'
  END                                AS "ecosystem",
  dep.key                            AS "package_name",
  COUNT(*)                           AS "occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(
       INPUT => CASE 
                  WHEN t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%' 
                  THEN PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require"
                  ELSE PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"dependencies"
                END
     ) dep
WHERE (t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%' OR t."sample_path" ILIKE '%package.json%')
  AND t."binary" = FALSE
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY "occurrences" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Top 20 Composer packages by total appearance count (all require & require-dev).
SELECT 
  dep.key                            AS "package_name",
  COUNT(*)                           AS "total_mentions"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(
       INPUT => OBJECT_AGG(
         'require',      PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require",
         'require-dev',  PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require-dev"
       )
     ) flat_outer,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => flat_outer.value) dep
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%'
  AND t."binary" = FALSE
GROUP BY dep.key
ORDER BY "total_mentions" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Packages that occur in BOTH require and require-dev of the same repo.
SELECT DISTINCT
  t."sample_repo_name",
  dep_req.key AS "package_name"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require")     dep_req,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require-dev") dep_dev
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%'
  AND dep_req.key = dep_dev.key
  AND t."binary" = FALSE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Full frequency list for all Composer "require" packages (to be consumed downstream).
SELECT 
  r.key   AS "package_name",
  COUNT(*) AS "frequency"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require") r
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json%'
  AND t."binary" = FALSE
GROUP BY r.key
ORDER BY "frequency" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
